WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.909 --> 00:00:05.220
Actress Shirley Henderson has a career that
spans well beyond a bathroom at Hogwarts,

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.000
and today, we're going to find out what she's
been doing since her stint in Harry Potter.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:15.460
From Korean films to acclaimed biopics, here's
what happened to the actress who played Moaning

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:15.960
Myrtle.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:17.460
"Who's Moaning Myrtle?"

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.180
"I'm Moaning Myrtle!"

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.160
When you rewatch the eight epic Harry Potter
films, it probably seems like every single

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.640
actor in the United Kingdom was in the cast,
including Shirley Henderson.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.580
She officially joined the series in its second
outing, 2002's Harry Potter and the Chamber

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.420
of Secrets, as the ghost known as Moaning
Myrtle.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.260
Despite having roles in previous box office
hits, like the romantic comedy Bridget Jones's

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.610
Diary and director Danny Boyle's breakthrough
film Trainspotting, Chamber of Secrets is

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.660
the movie that really put Henderson on the
map...and in the toilet.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:53.670
Moaning Myrtle, who died at Hogwarts years
before Harry started school, still haunts

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:58.600
the bathroom where she died, exacting revenge
on school bullies whenever she can find time

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.200
to take a break from sobbing.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.500
Despite her difficult nature, she actually
proves useful during her interactions with

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.000
Harry.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.240
In Chamber of Secrets, Harry eventually discovers
that the mythical monster of Slytherin house

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.800
is living in a hidden chamber directly beneath
Myrtle's bathroom and in Harry Potter and

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.980
the Goblet of Fire, she assists Harry as he
tries to decipher one of his tasks for the

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:23.310
Tri-wizard Tournament, even though she does
so while spying on the 14-year old while he

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.240
takes a bath.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.080
“Hello, Harry.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.700
Long time no see, oh!"

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.740
Perhaps the strangest part of Henderson's
Potter role is that she was 37 years old when

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.700
she first played the ghost of Myrtle.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.450
Immediately after exiting the Harry Potter
franchise in 2005, Shirley Henderson found

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:51.080
herself in a project fit for royalty — Sofia
Coppola's avant-garde Marie Antoinette.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:57.320
The 2006 film stars Kirsten Dunst as the doomed
queen of France, who enjoys a life of pure

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:02.200
excess before meeting a particularly grisly
end during the uprisings of the French Revolution.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:07.400
The film, which won an Academy Award for Best
Costume Design, features Henderson as Madame

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:12.170
Sophie, who is frequently at odds with Marie
Antoinette and constantly plotting against

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:13.340
the queen throughout her reign.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.980
Madame Sophie might not have been a leading
role, but it was an important one, proving

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:22.680
that Henderson was the perfect utility player
in everything from period pieces to blockbusters.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.820
After working on many successful theatrical
releases, Henderson joined the streaming revolution

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.020
and took a pivotal role in Netflix's Okja.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:37.040
The film is about a young girl and a super-pig,
whose DNA has been modified to make it a completely

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.700
unique animal and, unfortunately, a new food
source.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:47.090
The talented cast has huge stars including
Tilda Swinton, Jake Gyllenhaal, and Paul Dano.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.620
And, of course, there's Shirley Henderson
in a literal supporting role as the assistant

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.820
to Swinton's flighty CEO, Lucy Mirando.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:59.750
Besides being one of Netflix's most critically
praised films, the movie gave Henderson a

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.880
chance to give a stellar performance alongside
Swinton, even though their characters look

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.580
like seriously bad people.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:06.920
"Oh, we don't look too bad."

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.340
"We don't!?"

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:14.820
Shirley Henderson continued her strong run
in prestigious projects with 2018's Stan &amp; Ollie,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.800
which stars Oscar-nominee John C. Reilly as
Oliver Hardy and Steve Coogan as Stan Laurel.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.260
The film tells the story of the famed comedic
duo, as they struggle through personal and

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.820
professional problems near the end of their
careers.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:31.780
The roles of Laurel and Hardy's wives required
two talented actresses who wouldn't be diminished

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.220
to simple background players.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:39.100
Stan &amp; Ollie found that in Henderson, who
plays Lucille Hardy, and Nina Arianda, a Broadway

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.880
star who plays Ida Laurel.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:45.380
The two actresses brilliantly stand out in
the film, which isn't easy next to iconic

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.900
characters like Laurel and Hardy.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.500
"Such a wonderful reception, isn’t it, Ida?”

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.040
“It’s OK.”

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.140
“Two double acts for the price of one.”

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:59.480
Clearly, Shirley Henderson spent years making
a name for herself in big international projects,

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.420
but she always found time to return home and
work in highly regarded British television

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:03.920
dramas.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.880
Henderson kicked off this trend with 2013's
Southcliffe, a crime drama where she portrayed

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:11.740
a woman in the midst of a breakdown.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:16.720
Working alongside stars like Game of Thrones'
Joe Dempsie and Black Mirror's Rory Kinnear

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:21.070
as inhabitants of a small town grappling with
a series of violent shootings, the show was

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.760
a huge success for Henderson, earning her
a BAFTA nomination for the role.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:29.460
Continuing her pattern of choosing intense
characters, Henderson took on a supporting

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:34.650
role in Happy Valley as an unbalanced woman
with a lot of secrets and, apparently, not

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:35.660
a single umbrella.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:41.560
And in an extremely unexpected reunion, Henderson
appeared in Agatha Christie's The ABC Murders

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:46.120
with none other than Rupert Grint, her old
bathroom buddy from Harry Potter and the Chamber

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:46.620
of Secrets.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:51.280
But even after all these years, she still
can't quite get her mind out of the toilet.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:56.120
"I prefer my gentlemen not to be cavalier
with the use of the lavatory paper, it blocks

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:00.400
up the pipes and then you have to get in there
with a stick to break it up."

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:05.660
Plenty of actors jump at the chance to return
to the films that first brought them attention,

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:08.040
and Shirley Henderson is no exception.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:14.460
Back in 1996, Henderson had some very memorable
scenes in the original Trainspotting and in

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:19.020
2016, she got the chance to reunite with all
of the main cast members for a sequel.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.920
Henderson reprised her role as Gail, who married
her boyfriend, Spud, and had a child with

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:24.420
him.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.040
However, when Spud's addiction problems take
hold, Gail and her son leave him to figure

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.540
out his own recovery.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:35.620
Renton, played by Ewan McGregor, tries to
help Spud channel his addictive nature in

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:38.580
a more positive direction, with some mixed
results.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:42.830
Eventually, Spud gets his act together and
helps financially support Gail, but it's with

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:43.700
stolen money.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.320
As the film ends, it seems like the two might
be heading toward a lasting reunion.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:52.380
Although most of Henderson's scenes are with
Spud, we can't help but think that the actress

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:56.840
formerly known as "Moaning Myrtle" might have
a few more dirty secrets in common with Ewan

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:57.340
McGregor.

